## Direct Recommendation

Add a **quick-select chip row** above the existing `Selector` inside `ChatProfileSelector.vue`. It renders the top N profiles ranked by a usage metric (`usage_count`, `usage`, `count`, or `metrics.*`) and lets users toggle selection with a single click — no modal, no dropdown. Fall back to alphabetical order when no metrics are present, so it never renders empty.

---

## Specifications

| Dimension | Decision |
|---|---|
| **Layout** | `flex flex-col gap-2` wrapper; chip row is `flex flex-wrap gap-1.5` above the existing `Selector` |
| **Chip (default)** | `bg-white/5 text-white/60 border-white/10` → hover `bg-white/10 text-white/80` |
| **Chip (selected)** | `bg-primary/20 text-primary border-primary/40` |
| **Shape** | `rounded-full`, `px-2.5 py-1` (compact, won't fight the mini `ProfileCard`) |
| **Type** | `text-xs` label, `text-[10px]` icon — 14px+ avoided only because it's a compact inline tag |
| **States** | default → hover → `active:scale-95` (75ms) → `focus-visible:ring-2 ring-primary/50` → `aria-pressed` |
| **Transitions** | `duration-150` (fast) — matches micro-interaction standard |
| **Metric source** | `usage_count \|\| usage \|\| count \|\| metrics.usage \|\| metrics.count \|\| 0` |
| **Limit** | `quickProfilesLimit` prop, default `5` (keeps row to a single line on desktop) |

---

## Code

```vue src/components/chat/ChatProfileSelector.vue
<script setup>
import Selector from './Selector.vue'
import ProfileCard from '../ProfileCard.vue'
</script>

<template>
  <div class="flex flex-col gap-2">
    <!-- Quick select: top profiles by usage metric -->
    <div
      v-if="showQuickSelect && topProfiles.length"
      class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-1.5"
    >
      <span class="text-[10px] font-medium uppercase tracking-wider text-white/40 px-1">
        Quick
      </span>
      <button
        v-for="profile in topProfiles"
        :key="profile.name"
        type="button"
        :title="profile.name"
        :aria-pressed="isProfileSelected(profile)"
        class="inline-flex items-center gap-1.5 px-2.5 py-1 rounded-full border text-xs font-medium
               transition-all duration-150 active:scale-95
               focus:outline-none focus-visible:ring-2 focus-visible:ring-primary/50"
        :class="isProfileSelected(profile)
          ? 'bg-primary/20 text-primary border-primary/40'
          : 'bg-white/5 text-white/60 border-white/10 hover:bg-white/10 hover:text-white/80 hover:border-white/20'"
        @click="toggleProfile(profile)"
      >
        <i
          :class="profile.icon || 'fa-solid fa-user-astronaut'"
          class="text-[10px]"
          aria-hidden="true"
        ></i>
        <span class="truncate max-w-[120px]">{{ profile.name }}</span>
        <i
          v-if="isProfileSelected(profile)"
          class="fa-solid fa-check text-[10px]"
          aria-hidden="true"
        ></i>
      </button>
    </div>

    <Selector
      :items="profiles"
      :selected-items="selectedProfiles"
      label="Profiles"
      icon="fa-solid fa-plus"
      @update:selected-items="onProfilesSelected"
    >
      <!-- Custom profile card rendering in mini style -->
      <template #default="{ item, selected }">
        <div :class="selected ? 'ring-2 ring-primary rounded-lg' : 'rounded-lg'">
          <ProfileCard :profile="item" :mini="$ui.isMobile" />
        </div>
      </template>
    </Selector>
  </div>
</template>

<script>
export default {
  props: {
    project: {
      type: Object,
      default: null
    },
    openFromBottom: {
      type: Boolean,
      default: false
    },
    selectedProfiles: {
      type: Array,
      default: () => []
    },
    quickProfilesLimit: {
      type: Number,
      default: 5
    },
    showQuickSelect: {
      type: Boolean,
      default: true
    }
  },
  emits: ['update:selected-profiles', 'profiles-changed'],
  data() {
    return {
      profiles: []
    }
  },
  computed: {
    // Profiles ranked by usage metric (most used first, name as tie-breaker)
    rankedProfiles() {
      return [...this.profiles].sort((a, b) => {
        const diff = this.profileScore(b) - this.profileScore(a)
        return diff !== 0 ? diff : (a.name > b.name ? 1 : -1)
      })
    },
    topProfiles() {
      return this.rankedProfiles.slice(0, this.quickProfilesLimit)
    }
  },
  mounted() {
    this.loadProfiles(this.project || this.$project)
  },
  watch: {
    project: {
      handler(newProject) {
        if (newProject) {
          this.loadProfiles(newProject)
        }
      },
      immediate: true
    }
  },
  methods: {
    async loadProfiles(project) {
      try {
        if (project?.$api) {
          const profilesList = await project?.$api.profiles.list()
          this.profiles = (profilesList || []).sort((a, b) => a.name > b.name ? 1 : -1)
        }
      } catch (error) {
        console.error('[ChatProfileSelector] Error loading profiles:', error)
        this.profiles = []
      }
    },
    // Usage metric used to rank the quick selection (defensive against schema changes)
    profileScore(profile) {
      return profile?.usage_count
        || profile?.usage
        || profile?.count
        || profile?.metrics?.usage
        || profile?.metrics?.count
        || 0
    },
    // Selection key — works whether selectedProfiles holds names or objects
    profileKey(profile) {
      return typeof profile === 'string' ? profile : profile?.name
    },
    isProfileSelected(profile) {
      const name = profile?.name
      return this.selectedProfiles.some(p => this.profileKey(p) === name)
    },
    toggleProfile(profile) {
      const name = profile?.name
      if (!name) return
      const next = this.selectedProfiles.filter(p => this.profileKey(p) !== name)
      const wasSelected = next.length !== this.selectedProfiles.length
      if (!wasSelected) {
        next.push(name)
      }
      this.$emit('update:selected-profiles', next)
      this.$emit('profiles-changed', next)
    },
    onProfilesSelected(selectedItems) {
      this.$emit('update:selected-profiles', selectedItems)
      this.$emit('profiles-changed', selectedItems)
    }
  }
}
</script>
```

---

## Anti-Patterns to Avoid

- ❌ **A second source of truth for selection.** The quick chips MUST emit the same two events (`update:selected-profiles`, `profiles-changed`) so parents get one consistent state. Never keep a local `selected` array.
- ❌ **Assuming the metric field exists.** If backend schema changes, `profileScore` silently returns `0` and the list degrades to alphabetical — no crash, no empty row.
- ❌ **Locking `max-w` on the chip label incorrectly.** `truncate max-w-[120px]` keeps one-line rows; don't drop it or long profile names wrap and break the flow line.

---

## Accessibility Checklist

- [x] `aria-pressed` communicates selected/unselected toggle state to assistive tech.
- [x] `focus-visible:ring-2 ring-primary/50` — keyboard users get a clear, always-visible ring.
- [x] Selection is **not color-only** — a `fa-check` icon also indicates the active state.
- [x] Icon-only glyphs marked `aria-hidden="true"`; the profile name is the accessible label.
- [x] `title` provides a hover tooltip for truncated names.

---

## Implementation Steps

1. Replace the contents of `src/components/chat/ChatProfileSelector.vue` with the code above.
2. If the profiles API already exposes a usage/selection metric, wire it into `profileScore()` as the **first** fallback (e.g. `profile.selection_metrics?.[projectId]`).
3. Verify the parent passes `selectedProfiles` as an array (names); the `profileKey()` helper keeps it resilient to objects.
4. Toggle accessibility testing: press `Tab` to reach each chip, `Enter`/`Space` to flip selection, confirm ring is visible.
5. (Optional) Persist usage counts server-side on every `toggleProfile` so the "top" order actually converges over time — this is what makes the quick row *learn*.
